  "body": "Found in the second read of PR #3502 (head 8733e0621). Work this issue after that PR merges.\n\n1. The skip sentence (`crates/app/src/operation/cross_reach.rs:21-22`) says that the machine \"reaches it only from the side\". That is wrong for a hole along Z that opens downward (the case of #3448). It also says \"type it into a hole list by hand\". On a mill the only hole list is the Z list, so a user who does that gets a Z hole at the place of the radial hole. Keep only the correct advice: drill it in a setup that faces it.\n2. The doc comment at `crates/app/src/operation/material.rs:180-181` says \"Detection keeps those findings on a mill\". That is not true after PR #3502.\n3. `material.rs` has 425 lines (421 on `main`). Split it along the domain seam.\n4. `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md:25` does not say that a Drill operation on a mill names radial holes in `skipped`.\n5. No test covers detection in a rotated or aligned setup on a mill.\n6. Check what Generate does with a Drill operation that has a `cross` list on a plasma, waterjet or EDM machine. PR #3502 does not change that path. If it drills or passes with no message, file a defect.\n",
